  "interpretation": [
    "Distance and prior width describe who is compressed, including in the interior-prior sensitivity; this cannot uniquely identify public-news or Bayesian mechanisms.",
    "With month FE, prior-CPI equals prior up to a month constant. Stable selection and model-prior mathematical coupling prohibit causal interpretation; the stable-model R2 is not forecasting performance.",
    "Bayesian common-signal updating can predict more movement under a less precise prior. Actual respondents may not have seen the shared signal, may already know it, may use different horizons/consumption signals, or may repeat/hear/round the survey differently. Prior density IQR is only a proxy for precision, not calibrated inverse-variance information.",
    "Raw P contrasts can change after controls. No evidence supports fixing errors by simply adding points to demographic labels.",
    "Truth-stable group copy accuracy is partly guaranteed by selection. Threshold sensitivity uses finite reportable-month subsets; .25 correct-stable cells cover only eight months.",
    "Q8 also shows stable-person overmovement, so Q9 fitting alone cannot explain the entire pattern; Q8 and Q9 target different reported quantities."
  ],
